# Git

- Remote for this fork: `amixof` → `https://github.com/karbuunofficial/amixof-for-web.git`.
  Branch: `main`. (`origin` may point at upstream Stoat — never push there.)
- Before starting work: `git fetch amixof && git status`. If local `main` is behind, fast-forward
  (`git merge --ff-only amixof/main`) before editing. Never start on a stale tree; production may
  already run newer code than you have.
- Before deploying: commit, `git push amixof main`, confirm `git rev-parse HEAD` equals
  `git rev-parse amixof/main`.
- Production, GitHub `main`, and your local `main` should point at the same commit when you finish.
  If they do not, say which is ahead.

## Commits

- Conventional Commits (CI validates PR titles): `feat(scope): …`, `fix(scope): …`,
  `chore(scope): …`, `docs: …`, `refactor(scope): …`. Common scopes: `brand`, `auth`, `ui`,
  `settings`, `i18n`, `deploy`, `agents`.
- One logical change per commit. Body says *why*, lists user-visible effects, and notes anything
  not verified.
- Never commit: `.env*` (except `.env.example`), `.cursor/amixof.env`, `.cursor/artifacts/`,
  `dist/`, `node_modules/`, `styled-system/`, credentials, screenshots of signed-in user data.
- Never `--force` push `main`, never `git reset --hard` over someone else's pushed commits,
  never amend a commit that is already pushed.

## If git leaves lock files

If a command fails with "File exists … .lock", check no other git process is running
(`pgrep -l git`), then remove only that stale lock file.
